<template><div class="game-rules"><p class="rules-mode">ROYAL BLACKJACK · SIX DECKS</p><ol><li>Choose 0.50–20.00 credits in 0.50 steps. Cards come from six decks shuffled afresh for each hand. Aces count as 1 or 11; face cards count as 10.</li><li>HIT takes another card. STAND ends your turn. DOUBLE adds the same stake, deals one card, and stands. You can double on your first two cards, including after a split.</li><li>SPLIT a pair of the same rank once into two hands, adding the original stake. No resplitting. Split aces receive just one card each. A split-hand 21 is a normal win.</li><li>The dealer checks for blackjack before your decisions and stands on every 17, including soft 17. A natural is an ace plus a ten-value card on your original two-card hand. Both naturals tie.</li><li>Going over 21 loses. Otherwise, a higher total than the dealer, or a dealer bust, wins. Equal totals push. No insurance or surrender.</li></ol><table><thead><tr><th>Result</th><th>Profit</th><th>Total returned</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Natural blackjack</td><td>3:2</td><td>2.5× stake</td></tr><tr><td>Normal win</td><td>1:1</td><td>2× hand stake</td></tr><tr><td>Push</td><td>0</td><td>Hand stake returned</td></tr><tr><td>Lose / bust</td><td>−stake</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Split and double actions require sufficient available credits. Up to four times the initial stake can be committed (80.00 at the maximum). Active hand stakes are reserved and cannot be spent or redeemed elsewhere.</p><p>Your hand is saved. Reconnect to resume it. After five minutes without a decision, remaining hands automatically stand; the server processes the saved outcome when service activity resumes. The dealer’s hidden card and remaining shoe stay on the server.</p><p>This game uses its own approved test rules, stage-blackjack-v1. It does not use a fixed paying-round target. Guest previews do not change credits.</p></div></template>
